<!-- ============ TWO WAYS TO SELL WITH RFID ============ -->
<section class="ac-blue section" id="ways-to-sell">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-header">
      <div class="section-eyebrow">Two Ways to Sell</div>
      <h2 class="section-title">Two ways to sell with RFID.</h2>
      <p class="section-sub">Associate-guided at the counter or self-checkout on the floor. Both read the whole basket in one pass, with no line-of-sight scanning and no item-by-item barcode hunting.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="pillars-grid" style="grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);">
      <div class="pillar-card">
        <div class="pillar-icon"><i class="ti ti-device-tablet"></i></div>
        <h3 class="pillar-title">Associate-guided checkout</h3>
        <p class="pillar-desc">The basket goes near the antenna and the entire sale reads at once, so the receipt builds itself while the associate stays with the customer. Runs on the same <a href="/platform/mobile-pos/" style="color: var(--brand-text);">Mobile POS</a> the store already uses, anywhere on the floor.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pillar-card">
        <div class="pillar-icon"><i class="ti ti-scan"></i></div>
        <h3 class="pillar-title">RFID self-checkout</h3>
        <p class="pillar-desc">Items go in the bin and the cart appears on screen for the shopper to finish themselves. Confirmation logic and anti-bleed keep neighboring items off the receipt, and the EAS gates deactivate only what was paid for.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

