<!-- ============ FAQ ============ -->
<section class="ac-blue section" style="padding-bottom: 80px;">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-header">
      <div class="section-eyebrow">Frequently Asked Questions</div>
      <h2 class="section-title">RFID questions, answered.</h2>
    </div>
    <div style="max-width: 800px; margin: 0 auto;">
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question" onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('open')">
          What makes Teamwork Commerce RFID different from competitors?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>Teamwork Commerce offers the industry's only native end-to-end RFID stack, from tag encoding at receiving through checkout, loss prevention, and analytics. No third-party middleware required. New Black and NewStore offer unified commerce but require third-party integrations for deep RFID workflows. Our RFID is native to the core logic: every transaction (receiving, counting, transferring, selling) operates by individual EPC, not just UPC.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question" onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('open')">
          What is the unit control ledger?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>The unit control ledger provides a complete transactional history for every individual EPC, where it was commissioned, received, counted, transferred, sold, and whitelisted. It's the foundation for accurate Available-to-Sell data and for the blacklist/whitelist system that powers EAS gate integration. Think of it as a "license plate" tracking system for every unit in your inventory.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question" onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('open')">
          How does RFID loss prevention work with EAS gates?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>Every EPC in the store is blacklisted by default. When a unit is sold at POS, it's instantly whitelisted. The POS communicates with a local server in the store that holds a copy of the unit control ledger, which pushes the whitelist update to the EAS gates via API. The signal reaches the gate before the customer does. We integrate with Checkpoint, Sensormatic, and other gate providers.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question" onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('open')">
          What hardware do you support?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>We publish a certified hardware list covering the devices that are integrated and supported with TW POS Pro, including Bluebird RFID handhelds. Each device carries a certification status, the release it was introduced in, and the countries it is available in, and the whole list is reviewed every 120 days. We recommend certified hardware for full compatibility; if you want to use something not on the list, your Client Success team can advise on support.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question" onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('open')">
          Can vendors pre-tag items, or do we need to commission tags in-store?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>Both. If your vendor or warehouse ships goods already tagged, they scan straight into the purchase receipt. If not, Teamwork provides an integrated encoding workflow inside the purchase receipt document: define quantity, print and encode tags, affix them, then RFID scan to populate the receipt with individual EPCs. One step, no separate process.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

